==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|revolven||to change direction|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|revolver||to reflect upon|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|revolvere|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|revolvo|revolvō|turn over, roll back, reflect upon|lang=la}}, from {{term|re-||back|lang=la}} + {{term|volvo|volvō|roll|lang=la}}; see [[voluble]], [[volve]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|revolves|revolving|revolved}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To orbit a central point.
#: ''The Earth '''revolves''' around the sun.''
# To turn on an axis.
#: ''The Earth '''revolves''' once every twenty-four hours.''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To recur in cycles.
#: ''The program '''revolves''' through all the queues before returning to the start.''
#: ''The centuries '''revolve'''.''
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[ponder]] on, to [[reflect]] repeatedly upon, to [[consider]] all aspects of.
#* '''1843''', [[w:Thomas_Carlyle|Thomas Carlyle]], ''[[:w:Past and Present (book)|Past and Present]]'', book 2, ch. 6, ''Monk Samson''
#*: He sits silent, '''revolving''' many thoughts, at the foot of St. Edmund’s Shrine.

====Related terms====
* [[revolution]]
* [[revolver]]
* the world doesn't revolve around you

